=head2 SDL_hid_open

  my $result = SDL_hid_open($vendor_id, $product_id, $serial_number);

C: C<< SDL_hid_device * SDL_hid_open(unsigned short vendor_id, unsigned short product_id, const wchar_t * serial_number) >>

Open a HID device using a Vendor ID (VID), Product ID (PID) and optionally a serial number.

If `serial_number` is NULL, the first device with the specified VID and PID is opened.

=over

=item vendor_id - unsigned integer. the Vendor ID (VID) of the device to open.

=item product_id - unsigned integer. the Product ID (PID) of the device to open.

=item serial_number - reference to a scalar holding integer, pointer object or undef. the Serial Number of the device to open (Optionally NULL).

=back

Returns SDL3::HidDevice object or undef: a pointer to a SDL_hid_device object on success or NULL on failure; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

